      bearCase: "The bearish thesis focuses on persistent macroeconomic headwinds, including sticky inflation and aggressive interest rate hikes that continue to drain global liquidity. Further significant downturns in traditional equity markets, especially in major economic blocs, would likely drag down cryptocurrencies due to their increased correlation. Lingering regulatory uncertainty, or outright restrictive measures from major jurisdictions, could stifle growth and deter new entrants. Geopolitical instability and a global economic slowdown would also weigh heavily on investor confidence in risk assets.",
