      bearCase: "Geopolitical tensions in the Middle East re-escalate unexpectedly, leading to a sharp spike in oil prices and renewed supply disruption fears. Central banks are forced to maintain or intensify hawkish policies to combat inflation, triggering a global economic slowdown or recession. This combination results in a significant sell-off across equity and commodity markets.",
      neutralCase: "Markets remain in a state of cautious equilibrium. US-Iran tensions simmer without full resolution or major escalation, leading to sideways movement in oil prices. Central banks continue their data-dependent approach, making incremental policy adjustments. Economic data presents a mixed picture, preventing strong directional moves but avoiding a severe downturn, resulting in range-bound trading.",
      probabilityWeightedOutlook: "A probability-weighted outlook suggests a \'cautious optimism\' scenario with a 55% probability, where de-escalation holds, and markets slowly recover, but with lingering volatility. A \'re-escalation\' scenario holds a 30% probability, leading to significant downside. A \'stagnant equilibrium\' holds a 15% probability.",
